sample_tags.content_md:
## Site info tags

- `{{TITLE}}` : {{TITLE}} (page title)
- `{{FULL_TITLE}}` : {{FULL_TITLE}} (page title - site title)
- `{{UPDATE_DATE}}` : {{UPDATE_DATE}} (last updated date)
- `{{UPDATE_DATE:JP}}` : {{UPDATE_DATE:JP}} (last updated date, Japanese format)
- `{{UPDATE_DATE:SLASH}}` : {{UPDATE_DATE:SLASH}} (last updated date, slash-separated)
- `{{IS_NEW:30}}` : {{IS_NEW:30}} ("new" if within N days, empty otherwise)
- `{{DESCRIPTION}}` :{{DESCRIPTION}} (page description)
- `{{KEYWORDS}}` : {{KEYWORDS}} (page keywords)
- `{{OGP_IMAGE}}` : {{OGP_IMAGE}} (page thumbnail / OGP image URL)
- `{{PAGE_URL}}` : {{PAGE_URL}} (full URL of the page)
- `{{SITE_URL}}` : {{SITE_URL}} (site root URL)
- `{{SITE_NAME}}` : {{SITE_NAME}} (site title)
- `{{SITE_DESCRIPTION}}` : {{SITE_DESCRIPTION}} (site-wide description)
- `{{SITE_OGP_IMAGE}}` : {{SITE_OGP_IMAGE}} (site-wide OGP image URL)

---

## Image tag: `{{IMAGE:imageFileName}}`

```
Example: {{IMAGE:mikanBox.jpg}} — displays mikanBox.jpg
```

Just specify the filename — you don't need to worry about the path.

### Categories and images

When you upload an image while filtered to a category, the category name is automatically added as a filename prefix (e.g. blog_mikanBox.jpg).
This lets you keep images organized by category as you work. However, the prefix isn't added if the filename already starts with "_".

---

## Embedding a component: `{{COMPONENT:componentID}}`

Loads the component along with its CSS, fully scoped so it won't affect anything else.

```
Example: {{COMPONENT:_footer}} — embeds the footer component
```

{{COMPONENT:_footer}}

---

## Navigation (list-style page listing): NAV_LINKS

### All pages: `{{NAV_LINKS:all}}`

Displays the page list ordered by "sort order." Pages with a value below 0 are not shown.
The current page gets the `.active` class, so you can hide it or highlight it. Here it's highlighted in bold red.

```
Example: {{NAV_LINKS:all}}
```

{{NAV_LINKS:all}}

---

### Only links to pages with no category: `{{NAV_LINKS}}`

```
Example: {{NAV_LINKS}}
```

{{NAV_LINKS}}

---

### Filtered by category: `{{NAV_LINKS:category}}`

```
Example: {{NAV_LINKS:sample}} — only the "sample" category
```

{{NAV_LINKS:sample}}

---

## Card-style page listing: NAV_CARDS

### All pages: `{{NAV_CARDS:all}}`

Ordered by "sort order"; pages below 0 are not shown.
The current page gets the `.active` class, so you can hide it or highlight it. Here it's highlighted with an orange border.

```
Example: {{NAV_CARDS:all}}
```

{{NAV_CARDS:all}}

---

### Filtered by category: `{{NAV_CARDS:category}}`

```
Example: {{NAV_CARDS:sample}} — only the "sample" category
```

{{NAV_CARDS:sample}}

---

### Specifying a design: `{{NAV_CARDS:category:componentID}}`

Displays the cards using the design of the specified component.

```
Example: {{NAV_CARDS:sample:sample_card}}
```

{{NAV_CARDS:sample:sample_card}}

---

## Tags available inside a NAV_CARDS component

- `{{TITLE}}` : {{TITLE}} (page title)
- `{{UPDATE_DATE}}` : {{UPDATE_DATE}} (last updated date)
- `{{UPDATE_DATE:JP}}` : {{UPDATE_DATE:JP}} (last updated date, Japanese format)
- `{{UPDATE_DATE:SLASH}}` : {{UPDATE_DATE:SLASH}} (last updated date, slash-separated)
- `{{IS_NEW:30}}` : {{IS_NEW:30}} ("new" if within N days, empty otherwise)
- `{{DESCRIPTION}}` :{{DESCRIPTION}} (page description)
- `{{OGP_IMAGE}}` : {{OGP_IMAGE}} (page thumbnail / OGP image URL)
- `{{PAGE_URL}}` : {{PAGE_URL}} (full URL of the page)
- `{{IS_ACTIVE}}` : {{IS_ACTIVE}} (whether this is the page currently being viewed)
- `{{POST_MD::key}}` : {{POST_MD::key}} (displays embedded data)
- `{{POST_MD::#rowID:key}}` : {{POST_MD::#rowID:key}} (displays embedded tabular data)

---

## Everything from here on is for advanced users — no need to memorize it right away.

---

## Embedding Markdown from another page: `{{POST_MD:pageID}}`

```
Example: {{POST_MD:sample_md}}
```

↓ starting from the line below

{{POST_MD:sample_md}}

↑ up to the line above

---

## Embedding Markdown from an external site: `{{EXT_MD:url}}`

※ **Not available in the Cloud edition.**

You can embed and display data from places like GitHub.
For security reasons, JavaScript will not execute.

```
Example: {{EXT_MD:https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yoshihik0/testData/main/md-test-e.md}}
```

[GitHub page](https://github.com/yoshihik0/testData/blob/main/md-test-e.md)

↓ starting from the line below

{{EXT_MD:https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yoshihik0/testData/main/md-test-e.md}}

↑ up to the line above

---

## Defining data: `{{DATA:key}}value{{/DATA}}`

Like WordPress custom fields, you can define data under a named key.

```
{{DATA:key}}value{{/DATA}} : defines data (shown)
{{DATA:key:GHOST}}value{{/DATA}} : defines data (hidden via GHOST)
```

```
Example:
### {{DATA:BOOK_TITLE}}Programming PHP{{/DATA}}
Author: {{DATA:AUTHOR}}Taro Yamada{{/DATA}}
{{DATA:ISBN:GHOST}}978-1234567890{{/DATA}}
```
Define data using this format. Here's how it's rendered on the page:
Since ISBN is set to GHOST, it isn't displayed.
It works like a form's `type="hidden"` attribute.

### {{DATA:BOOK_TITLE}}Programming PHP{{/DATA}}
Author: {{DATA:AUTHOR}}Taro Yamada{{/DATA}}
Price: ¥{{DATA:PRICE}}2800{{/DATA}}
{{DATA:ISBN:GHOST}}978-1234567890{{/DATA}}

---

## Displaying defined data

### Displaying data from within the same page: `{{POST_MD::key}}`

Displays the data defined above.

```
Example:
{{POST_MD::BOOK_TITLE}}
{{POST_MD::AUTHOR}}
{{POST_MD::ISBN}}
```

{{POST_MD::BOOK_TITLE}}
{{POST_MD::AUTHOR}}
{{POST_MD::ISBN}}

Even data hidden with GHOST when it was defined can still be read and displayed elsewhere.

---

### Displaying data from another page: `{{POST_MD:pageID:key}}`

Displays the data defined on the sample_data page.

```
Example:
{{POST_MD:sample_data:AUTHOR}}
{{POST_MD:sample_data:BOOK_TITLE}}
```
{{POST_MD:sample_data:AUTHOR}}
{{POST_MD:sample_data:BOOK_TITLE}}

---

### Displaying data from an external site: `{{EXT_MD:url:key}}`

※ **Not available in the Cloud edition.**

```
Example:
{{EXT_MD:https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yoshihik0/testData/main/data-test.md:BOOK}}
{{EXT_MD:https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yoshihik0/testData/main/data-test.md:AUTHOR}}
```

{{EXT_MD:https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yoshihik0/testData/main/data-test.md:BOOK}}
{{EXT_MD:https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yoshihik0/testData/main/data-test.md:AUTHOR}}

[GitHub page](https://github.com/yoshihik0/testData/blob/main/data-test.md)

---

## Defining a database

### `{{DATAROW:rowID}}　{{DATA:key}}value{{/DATA}}　{{/DATAROW}}`

```
Example:
{{DATAROW:menu1}}          : think of "menu1" as a spreadsheet row
{{DATA:ITEM}}Pasta{{/DATA}}  : defines ITEM=Pasta
{{DATA:PRICE}}1200{{/DATA}}  : defines PRICE=1200
{{/DATAROW}}

{{DATAROW:menu2}}          : think of "menu2" as a spreadsheet row
{{DATA:ITEM}}Soup{{/DATA}}   : defines ITEM=Soup
{{DATA:PRICE}}700{{/DATA}}   : defines PRICE=700
{{/DATAROW}}
```

{{DATAROW:menu1}}
{{DATA:ITEM}}Pasta{{/DATA}}
{{DATA:PRICE}}1200{{/DATA}}
{{/DATAROW}}
{{DATAROW:menu2}}
{{DATA:ITEM}}Soup{{/DATA}}
{{DATA:PRICE}}700{{/DATA}}
{{/DATAROW}}

---

